      "side": 1,
      "message": "(Actually it\u0027s not simply a rounding issue, my commit message is not clear enough)\nDIV_ROUND works in this case, but might not for future devices.\n\nUse the numbers in the commit message as an example. \n\nRounding means shifting the allowed dpi range from [800, 801) to [799.5, 800.5).\n254 * LOGICAL_MAX_Y / PHYSICAL_MAX_Y \u003d 799.9895 lies inside the new interval, this is good.\n\nHowever, increasing PHYSICAL_MAX_Y by 1 means the computed dpi will be decreased by 1.3 (801.3 -\u003e 799.9). The step is larger than our acceptable range, so it\u0027s very likely that we still can\u0027t find integer solution of PHYSICAL_MAX_Y for some LOGICAL_MAX_Y.\n\nMy code here is trying to triple the allowed range from [800, 801) to [799, 802), so that if dpi and LOGICAL_MAX_X is still close to the current value, the integer solution exists.",
